# Normalise line endings in the repository. Windows checkouts wrote CRLF while
# Linux wrote LF, so git saw every line of README.md, WHATS-INSIDE.md and
# start.cmd as changed and raised whole-file conflicts whose two sides were
# byte-identical once normalised. Storing LF ends that class of conflict.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files need CRLF on disk to be safe for cmd.exe.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
